earch Awards\nCampus Life\nNews and Events\nVideos\nContact\nGraduate & Postdoctoral Studies\nSpencer Engineering Building\nRoom 2079\nWestern University\nweadmit@uwo.ca\nAwards and Scholarships\nWestern Engineering offers financial support for eligible research-based (PhD and MESc) graduate students who achieve a minimum average of 78% at the time of admission. To continue receiving funding, students are required to maintain a minimum average of 70%. Financial support is provided through research grants, contracts, scholarships, and teaching assistantships. Eligible research-based students will receive a minimum of $13,000 plus tuition (excluding ancillary fees) from all sources. After a PhD student completes their Comprehensive exam, the minimum financial support package will increase to a minimum of $14,000 plus tuition (excluding ancillary fees). For information about the cost of living and educational expenses while at Western, please visit our Financial Planning page.\nStudents are encouraged to review all opportunities available and apply to those for which you are eligible.\nInternships\nScholarships:\nExternal Scholarships\nInternal Scholarships\nGraduate and Postdoctoral Studies\nFuture Students\nCurrent Students\nPostdoctoral Studies\nExperiential Learning\nInternational Students\nAcademic Support\nCareer Services\nWellness Resources\nAwards and Scholarships\nExternal Scholarships\nInternal Scholarships\nIBET Fellowship\nInternship / Work Placement\nScholarsheet (Doctoral Awards)\nGraduate Awards\nUndergraduate Summer Research Awards\nCampus Life\nNews and Events\nVideos\n\u00a9 1878 - Western University\nWestern Engineering\nSpencer Engineering Building, Western University\nLondon, Ontario, Canada, N6A 5B9\nTel: 519-661-2111\ncontactWE@eng.uwo.ca\nPrivacy |\nWeb Standards |\nTerms of Use |\nAccessibility\nKey Topics:\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nResearch\nIndustry\nAlumni\nDepartments\nPopular Resources:\nWestern Mail\nBrightspace\nStudent Services\nWestern